## Summary

I found and fixed an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The bug was that the function was returning `parts[1]` (the second word) instead of `parts[0]` (the first word). This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail: returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error: IndexError when trying to access index 1 in a single-element list

The fix was simple: changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass successfully.
